{"id": "De17nUjosQl", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "No human has EVER climbed Mount Kailash 🏔️ Everest has been climbed 13,000+ times. Kailash? ZERO. Here’s why 👇\n\n🏔️ Mount Kailash (6,638 m) is about 2 km shorter than Everest (8,849 m), yet there is no known ascent of it, ever.\n🔱 For Hindus it is the home of Lord Shiva, the mountain Ravana once lifted. It is sacred to Buddhists, Jains and Bon too.\n🌊 Four great rivers begin near it: the Indus, the Sutlej, the Brahmaputra and the Karnali.\n🧗 In the 1980s, Reinhold Messner, the first man to climb all 14 of the world’s highest peaks, was offered the chance. He refused: “If we conquer this mountain, then we conquer something in people’s souls.”\n🚫 Today, climbing Kailash is forbidden.\n\nSo pilgrims don’t climb it. They walk AROUND it 🙏\n👣 The Kailash kora (parikrama) is over 50 km long and crosses the Dolma La pass at about 5,630 m. Hindus, Buddhists and Jains walk it clockwise, keeping Shiva on their right. It’s pradakshina, around Shiva’s own home.\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods’ stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. 15K FAMILY DEAL: Books 1–3 for ₹350 (was ₹500), only till 25 Oct midnight. Comment FAMILY and we’ll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio → rishikatha.com\n\n💬 Has anyone in YOUR family done the Kailash yatra? Comment your city!\n🔖 Save this, and send it to the person in your family who dreams of going to Kailash.\n\n#kailash #mountkailash #kailashmansarovar #kailashyatra #harharmahadev mahadev shiva lordshiva parikrama pradakshina sanatandharma hinduism himalayas rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792771145, "like_count": 31918, "comment_count": 143, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1088915380435089a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 58.367, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none",